      "id": "s1",
      "nodeId": "n1",
      "text": "The 8-second attention span is not the only myth about human attention.",
      "contextBefore": "nds familiar, therefore it is true. In fact, no one knows how to actually measure a goldfish's attention span. What has been measured by researchers is goldfish memory, which, is actually quite good. ",
      "contextAfter": " Several authors claim that attention span declines precipitously after 10-15 min. As a result of those claims, it is often suggested that presentations/lectures/talks should last no more than 10-15 m",
      "start": 2192,
      "end": 2263,
      "extractSha256": "da19f58d7cc546fd04beaaa3a302a4749105cbdd80276a5263b1953ec274f8a6",
