      "id": "s4",
      "nodeId": "n4",
      "text": "Publishers are now rolling out shorter books faster and faster, and Harvard Business School historian Nancy Koehn says it's largely because we're getting less attentive and more anxious: \"The average American attention span in 2013 was about 8 seconds.",
